# Deploy exar via ssh t3

**Timestamp:** 2026-07-28

## Task
Fix remote Docker deploy target and deploy `exar` to Irancell-T3 (`ssh t3`).

## Commands
- Inspected `~/.ssh/config` Host `t3` and verified `ssh t3`
- Fixed `.armin/docker-scripts/run-on-docker-server.yaml`: `ssh: "ssh t3 -p 80"` → `ssh: "ssh t3"`
- Built linux binary: `CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build -o bin/server ./cmd/server`
- Ran `.\.armin\docker-scripts\run-on-docker-server.ps1`

## Important outputs
- Wrong SSH port 80 caused deploy failure (HTTP/HAProxy, not SSH)
- `bin/server` was missing; rebuilt before image build
- Remote compose up succeeded on `/home/cloud-admin/docker/exar` using network `t3-net`

## Result
Deploy succeeded. Containers `exar-webui` and `exar-api` started on `t3`.

## Warnings
- Do not set `ssh` to `-p 80`; SSH uses port 22 via Host `t3` in `~/.ssh/config`
- Dockerfile expects prebuilt `bin/server` (linux/amd64) and `dist/`
